BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 653.77 Tm (The most expensive mistake on the board is a disposal shortcut. Imperial Brady warns that if spill materials) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 638.55 Tm (get tossed into a dumpster, the entire dumpster becomes hazardous waste and the facility is charged) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 623.32 Tm (accordingly; without in-house guidelines, infectious materials go to a licensed biohazard disposal company) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 608.10 Tm ([tCz-yNw0WBo @ 00:08:08]. Mary Doha's municipal program shows the clean version of that pipeline: filled) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 592.87 Tm (sharps containers go into a square cardboard box from the vendor kept in a storage closet, a box that might) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 577.65 Tm (take a year to fill for a town department versus a week in a hospital, and the vendor pickup comes with a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 562.42 Tm (waste manifest naming the medical incinerator, a cradle-to-grave paper trail [4xmWcKLIfmA @ 00:24:38].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 547.20 Tm (The same webinar bans the household workaround at work: residents may use an old laundry detergent or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 531.97 Tm (Gatorade bottle, but a workplace crew must use an official hard-shell sharps container [4xmWcKLIfmA @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 516.75 Tm (00:23:52]. BuddSafety adds that disposal is site-specific, so every account should have a way to get rid of a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 501.52 Tm (biohazard bag, and the tech contacts the manager with any question [eEnUgYz8rXU @ 00:04:59]. Imperial) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 486.30 Tm (Brady's fallback when no kit bag exists is a disposable bag set inside a secondary rigid container, sealed,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 471.07 Tm (and handled only with gloves on.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 455.85 Tm (Sharps traps are where the punctures actually happen. Mary Doha describes sharps containers stuffed with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 440.62 Tm (bottle caps, tin foil and baggies until the next needle fell back out onto someone's hand, so non-sharps go in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 425.40 Tm (regular trash even though mixing them in is not against the law [4xmWcKLIfmA @ 00:17:57]. The same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 410.17 Tm (webinar lists the handling errors that create sticks: holding the container in one hand while feeding a syringe) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 394.95 Tm (with the other, recapping a bare needle, walking a syringe back to the truck instead of bringing the container) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 379.72 Tm (to the find, and passing a syringe hand to hand rather than setting it on a flat surface [4xmWcKLIfmA @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 364.50 Tm (00:14:32]. Glove buying carries its own trap: healthcare latex lets needle tips go right through, and the bright) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 349.27 Tm (orange coating the trainers first took for the puncture feature on a sample glove turned out to be grip only,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 334.05 Tm (with the real protection a pad sewn into the palm [4xmWcKLIfmA @ 00:13:45]. For janitorial crews the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 318.82 Tm (hidden needle is the threat: The Janitorial Store warns that improperly discarded needles get concealed in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 303.60 Tm (linen or garbage and injure workers who meet them unexpectedly [U5pnasmmPuY @ 00:04:27].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 288.37 Tm (Post-exposure mistakes and training churn are the last traps. Mary Doha tells stuck workers to wash with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 273.15 Tm (soap and water only, never bleach or disinfectant on skin, because damaged skin transmits HIV and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 257.92 Tm (hepatitis more easily; notify the supervisor immediately rather than at end of shift, and get a medical exam) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 242.70 Tm (within 24 hours at a pre-selected occupational health provider or ER, since some personal doctors have not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 227.47 Tm (seen a needle stick in ten years [4xmWcKLIfmA @ 00:39:05]. The employer may get the bill, a $45 hepatitis) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 212.25 Tm (test from the ER, but results go only to the worker, and the syringe stays out of the exam room because) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 197.02 Tm (there is not enough blood in it to test [4xmWcKLIfmA @ 00:41:52]. BuddSafety admits its demo crew) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 181.80 Tm (skipped full PPE because the blood was ketchup, and notes not all kits are the same, so crews follow) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 166.57 Tm (whatever box their site stocks [eEnUgYz8rXU @ 00:06:16]. On the labor side, Keep It Clean runs the math:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 151.35 Tm (training is annual, and a 100-employee company with even a low 200 percent turnover still pushes 300) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 136.12 Tm (people through it in a year [8EjRhmcPsz0 @ 00:04:06]. That churn is why the hosts treat the course price) Tj ET
